{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast","id":558257,"title":"Possible problem with the upgraded Giant merit in Beast","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-17T08:04:38-07:00","id":558257,"title":"Possible problem with the upgraded Giant merit in Beast","content":"As written the Giant merit gets more powerful the higher your Satiety gets, which means that it works in the exact opposite way that Atavisms do, despite functionally <i>being</i> an Atavism (regardless of how it ended up organized into the book). I like the overall idea of having a character whose real size is expressed in more than just the impression of size and strength, but I feel like the bits that say 'Satiety' in the Merit description ought to be altered to '10 - Satiety' or something similar.<br /> <br /> The overall game would probably also be better served by having this Merit changed to an actual Atavism as well, but that's possibly a matter of perception. The only reason I can think of to put it into the Merit category is so a character can take it without sacrificing one of their other Atavism picks.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any thoughts, better suggestions, etc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T08:28:24-07:00","id":558290,"title":"","content":"I think it works fine. Higher satiety - more mass (a full belly). Plus all it's effects are to do with inertia and not being knocked down. Exactly how a full Horror acts. Go ahead, hit them with a car, they ain't going <i>nowhere. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T08:55:32-07:00","id":558314,"title":"","content":"Lets flip the question around - what does it hurt to have it as a merit instead of a Persistant Atavism? What benefit is there? If we made it into an atavism, we'd need to have it take effect with Low Satiety and a Satiety expenditure, and this way we have a way to have the effect without any unwanted additions. This way, we're able to convey the impression Elfive mentioned (full = heavy and unmovable), since its thematic. Atavisms tend to want you at low Satiety, which is not the intent of the merit.<br /> <br /> As well, right now, we have a nice round number of four Atavisms per Family. If we made this into a fifth, then we'd need more for the others as well... and things just get messier from there. And, if we turn Giant into an atavism... why not do the same for Direction Sense? Striking Looks? Pretty much all the Advanced and Epic merits can be dealt with that way.<br /> <br /> You said that turning the merit into an atavism would benefit the game.... how? I don't see how it hurts the game, and I can see some benefit to leaving it as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T10:27:29-07:00","id":558399,"title":"","content":"My central point was the actual mechanic and not the classification. I don't really care if it is considered an Atavism or not. (I think it'd be better off in the Atavism section mainly because I spent about 10 minutes yesterday trying to find it again. I didn't remember the name and it is a case of a physical effect based on your Soul body echoing into the material world, so I was wracking my brain trying to figure out if I was just imagining the effect or skimming past it somehow.)<br /> <br /> The higher Satiety=heavier thing would make better sense if if it weren't for the fact that the logic of everything else in the game that has a similar mechanism works in the exact <i>opposite</i> fashion. Even the other abilities specifically related to size and strength get stronger and more pronounced the hungrier you are, and fade when sated. It just feels backward in the context of the rest of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T10:37:05-07:00","id":558410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558399#post558399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the other abilities specifically related to size and strength get stronger and more pronounced the hungrier you are, and fade when sated. It just feels backward in the context of the rest of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looming Presence's only addition at low Satiety is that you get <i>scarier</i> and Cyclopean Strength only makes it so you can swing things around better. The nearest we get to what you're describing is Titanic Blow, which is hardly a plural unto itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T10:58:20-07:00","id":558437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558410#post558410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looming Presence's only addition at low Satiety is that you get <i>scarier</i> and Cyclopean Strength only makes it so you can swing things around better. The nearest we get to what you're describing is Titanic Blow, which is hardly a plural unto itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looming Presence makes you scarier because you seem larger, Cyclopean Strength makes you physically stronger, Titanic Blow transmits the force of your massive punches more effectively. All three are amplified by low Satiety and the IC mechanism for all three is that you're more strongly tied to the massive size and strength of your other self while you're hungry.<br /> <br /> Most of the other physical Atavisms work the same way when you're at low Satiety. Limb From Limb deepens the impact of your claws, Monster from the Deep behaves more clearly like deadly tentacles, Infestation turns you from merely malleable into a barely-coherent swarm thing, the poison of Basilisk's Touch grows more concentrated, Relentless Hunter shoves aside the basic needs of your frail human shell, Unbreakable visibly hardens you against harm....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T11:48:34-07:00","id":558516,"title":"","content":"It doesn't matter how Atavisms work. It's a Merit. It would make no sense to get heavier as you got hungrier. There is no problem. Plus, if this would have to be an Atavism, then so would the Directional Sense, Iron Skin, Killer Insinct and any other Merit that is Beast specific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T11:51:26-07:00","id":558517,"title":"","content":"Atavism effects and Beast-only merits don't need to work on the same logic. To put it in another way, the way Advanced Giant functions doesn't cause conflict in influencing factors with the more physical Atavisms, although they're opposite.*<br /> <br /> Atavisms become stronger when the Soul is hungry because that sharpens its focus, causing more power to seep into the Begotten's body. Meanwhile, Advanced Giant draws on the Beast's Satiety itself, with it having an effect on her physical mass depending on how full the Soul is.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*I swear this explanation sounded less awkward in my head. Hmm.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-17-2015, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T12:02:29-07:00","id":558521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558399#post558399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The higher Satiety=heavier thing would make better sense if if it weren't for the fact that the logic of everything else in the game that has a similar mechanism works in the exact <i>opposite</i> fashion. Even the other abilities specifically related to size and strength get stronger and more pronounced the hungrier you are, and fade when sated. It just feels backward in the context of the rest of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div> But those things make sense. If you're hungry, you have more ambition and drive, while feeding makes you more food-coma-ish. &quot;You're hungry for victory!&quot; means you push yourself harder; hunger, in general, is a metaphor for a strong desire and a willingness to go far to satisfy those desires. Meanwhile, being well fed is associated with sloth and inertia; a fat cat, if you will. Two different feelings we're evoking in either case.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T12:07:12-07:00","id":558526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558516#post558516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't matter how Atavisms work. It's a Merit. It would make no sense to get heavier as you got hungrier. There is no problem. Plus, if this would have to be an Atavism, then so would the Directional Sense, Iron Skin, Killer Insinct and any other Merit that is Beast specific.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how the majority of Beasts feed it doesn't make any sense to get heavier as they feed either, and certainly not to the degree that the merit implies their mass increases. If you've got the Prey hunger and eat babies that's one thing, but if you steal Faberge eggs or publicly embarrass adulterers, suddenly gaining 400lbs of entirely psychic weight makes absolutely no sense.<br /> <br /> I am not saying that this <i>HAS</i> to be an Atavism, or even that it necessarily <i>should</i> be. I am saying that the metaphysical reasoning for what is happening with the Giant upgrade seems to be the same as the Atavism powers in that it is a physical effect on your human body as a result of the presence of your Soul, and because of that having it work in the opposite direction doesn't appear to fit. I honestly assumed that was written based on an earlier revision of the rules where Satiety worked differently and had just been overlooked, which is why I brought it up in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T12:17:16-07:00","id":558532,"title":"","content":"Also, the main reason I haven't brought up the other merits you've all mentioned is that they don't scale on Satiety. Admittedly some of them (especially Iron Skin) could definitely fall into the same thematic category, there isn't enough mechanical similarity that they seem like an actual oversight to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T12:21:24-07:00","id":558535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558521#post558521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But those things make sense. If you're hungry, you have more ambition and drive, while feeding makes you more food-coma-ish. &quot;You're hungry for victory!&quot; means you push yourself harder; hunger, in general, is a metaphor for a strong desire and a willingness to go far to satisfy those desires. Meanwhile, being well fed is associated with sloth and inertia; a fat cat, if you will. Two different feelings we're evoking in either case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of the difference of opinion on this is that I'm interpreting this more as the Juggernaut and you (and obviously a number of others) are interpreting it more along the lines of the Blob. (the mutant, not the jello that eats people)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T13:10:54-07:00","id":558616,"title":"","content":"OP is absolutely right.<ul><li>Being hungry makes the monster manifest itself.</li> <li>The merit makes the monster manifest itself.</li> <li>Ergo, the merit should manifest itself when you get hungry to maintain thematic consistency.</li> </ul>It would also make a neat Atavism for Giants and Dragons and Kraken and Godzilla and similar monsters.<br /> But that's not strictly necessary - Looming Presence is already fairly decent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 06-17-2015, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T13:12:26-07:00","id":558618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558526#post558526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given how the majority of Beasts feed it doesn't make any sense to get heavier as they feed either, and certainly not to the degree that the merit implies their mass increases.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes complete sense. The Soul(Horror) has fed. Feeding makes you heavier. It doesn't matter if the Beast is actually <i>eating</i> anything because Satiety has nothing to do with the Beasts actually body. The Soul(Horror) is what was fed and <i>that</i> is what is making you heavier. If gaining 400 lbs of psychic weight makes no sense to you, then how does making it happen at low satiety make anymore sense? It's still not actual body mass. It is not the Beast that has actually grown heavy, it's their Soul(Horror). Just like it's not <i>really</i> the Beast picking up a garbage truck, it's actually the Soul(Horror) doing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T13:17:56-07:00","id":558627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558616#post558616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OP is absolutely right.<ul><li>Being hungry makes the monster manifest itself.</li> <li>The merit makes the monster manifest itself.</li> <li>Ergo, the merit should manifest itself when you get hungry to maintain thematic consistency.</li> </ul>It would also make a neat Atavism for Giants and Dragons and Kraken and Godzilla and similar monsters.<br /> But that's not strictly necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Beast manifests itself when your not hungry too. See almost <i>every</i> Atavism. Plus, Looming Presence already cover s huge monsters. Being size 7+ is going to make you pretty hard to move in it's own right. Giant(Advanced) just represents another way to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T13:27:03-07:00","id":558653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558627#post558627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Beast manifests itself when your not hungry too. See almost <i>every</i> Atavism. Plus, Looming Presence already cover s huge monsters. Being size 7+ is going to make you pretty hard to move in it's own right. Giant(Advanced) just represents another way to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Beast manifests <b>MORE</b> when you are hungry.<br /> The Beast manifests <b>LESS</b> when you are full.<br /> Only Nightmares get better when your Beast is sleepy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 06-17-2015, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T14:53:40-07:00","id":558771,"title":"","content":"It could go either way, but the way it does work seems like Merit is the right place for it. The connection to the Horror doesn't grow stronger at any point. There is a connection. As the Beast's Satiety increases the Horror has more &quot;weight.&quot; If it was reworked based on a connection that varied in strength then increasing Satiety would likely weaken the Giant. If you think of it more like an Atavism then it seems off. If you just look at it as a Merit then you see that there is just a connection and Satiety affects how that connection expresses itself, but this all works in a completely different fashion than an Atavism. The &quot;Giant&quot; manifestation never increases or decreases it just changes, hence it is a Merit. They started out by saying how can we make this Merit linked to the Horror, and not how a Beast/Horror connection would affect a Beast's substance based on Satiety. If you go front to back it looks weird, go back to front and it makes sense. It is just one of life's fun little happenstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T15:32:44-07:00","id":558803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558653#post558653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Beast manifests <b>MORE</b> when you are hungry.<br /> The Beast manifests <b>LESS</b> when you are full.<br /> Only Nightmares get better when your Beast is sleepy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The poiny was that it doesn't matter. You are applying the rules of Atavisms to a Merit. That's foolish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T15:58:53-07:00","id":558813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558771#post558771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you go front to back it looks weird, go back to front and it makes sense. It is just one of life's fun little happenstances.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558803#post558803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The poiny was that it doesn't matter. You are applying the rules of Atavisms to a Merit. That's foolish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at it like an Atavism makes the most thematic sense, because Atavisms have a strong connection to the physicality of the Beast itself. Your physicality is exactly what the Merit addresses. If that physicality were static, or associated with something like Lair, then there would be no issue and that would be a completely valid solution. But right now the merit actually causes you to gain mass when you increase in Satiety, which is counter to the established thematic that has been created around the gain and loss of Satiety.<br /> <br /> Which makes more sense to you?<br /> That you steadily gain mass along with your other bestial traits as you approach Satiety 0?<br /> Or that you steadily gain mass as you lose your other bestial traits, then suddenly lose all that mass the moment you hit Satiety 10?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T16:20:48-07:00","id":558825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558813#post558813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which makes more sense to you?<br /> That you steadily gain mass along with your other bestial traits as you approach Satiety 0?<br /> Or that you steadily gain mass as you lose your other bestial traits, then suddenly lose all that mass the moment you hit Satiety 10?</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize you just said you get bigger when you don't eat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T16:28:26-07:00","id":558830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558825#post558825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do realize you just said you get bigger when you don't eat.</div> </div> </div> </div>You become more <b>monstrous</b> when you don't eat.<br /> This is a <b>monster</b> merit.<br /> You <b>lose</b> your monster merits when you eat too much<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T16:34:08-07:00","id":558833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558813#post558813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at it like an Atavism makes the most thematic sense, because Atavisms have a strong connection to the physicality of the Beast itself. Your physicality is exactly what the Merit addresses. If that physicality were static, or associated with something like Lair, then there would be no issue and that would be a completely valid solution. But right now the merit actually causes you to gain mass when you increase in Satiety, which is counter to the established thematic that has been created around the gain and loss of Satiety.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at it like an Atavism makes no sense because<i><b> it is not an Atavism</b></i>. It makes the most thematic sense that<i> as you eat you get heavier,</i> because thats what actually happens when you eat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558813#post558813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which makes more sense to you?<br /> That you steadily gain mass along with your other bestial traits as you approach Satiety 0?<br /> Or that you steadily gain mass as you lose your other bestial traits, then suddenly lose all that mass the moment you hit Satiety 10?</div> </div> </div> </div>The later. Firstly, because all of you Beast traits do not get stronger as you get hungrier, <i>only</i> Atavisms do. Nightmares get stronger.<br /> Secondly, because it makes <i>no sense in any way</i> to say you get <b>heavier</b> as you <i>starve</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T17:08:37-07:00","id":558871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558833#post558833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at it like an Atavism makes no sense because<i><b> it is not an Atavism</b></i>. It makes the most thematic sense that<i> as you eat you get heavier,</i> because thats what actually happens when you eat. The later. Firstly, because all of you Beast traits do not get stronger as you get hungrier, <i>only</i> Atavisms do. Nightmares get stronger.<br /> Secondly, because it makes <i>no sense in any way</i> to say you get <b>heavier</b> as you <i>starve</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you are just stuck on the idea that this involves physical food? That is only the case sometimes.<br /> You also have not reconciled the thematic issue that <i><b>you lose all that mass the second you hit Satiety 10.</b></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T17:28:48-07:00","id":558882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558871#post558871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you are just stuck on the idea that this involves physical food? That is only the case sometimes.<br /> You also have not reconciled the thematic issue that <i><b>you lose all that mass the second you hit Satiety 10.</b></i></div> </div> </div> </div>I am not stuck on the ides that it involves actual food. I have previously stated that it does not involve actual food. That has <i>nothing</i> to do with the concept of getting heavier as you eat. You Soul is the thing getting fat.<br /> <br /> You loose all the extra mass at Satiety 10...so? You loose all your Beast powers at Satiety 10, including the other ones that get more powerful as you fill up. There is no thematic issue with this, because it has nothing to do with the themes of a specific power, it affects <i>all</i> powers the same. That would only be relevant if that only happened with this one specific power. It doesn't though.<br /> <br /> You are stuck on the idea that it a &quot;should&quot; function s an Atavism. It does not and it should not. The idea of getting heavier when starving is ridiculous and completely counter to the point <i>and</i> theme of the Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T17:42:21-07:00","id":558890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558833#post558833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at it like an Atavism makes no sense because<i><b> it is not an Atavism</b></i>. It makes the most thematic sense that<i> as you eat you get heavier,</i> because thats what actually happens when you eat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fear does not have a weight. There's no reason why consuming it should make you heavier, except that the Soul is manifesting itself more strongly. The Soul shouldn't be manifesting itself if you're at high satiety.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558825#post558825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do realize you just said you get bigger when you don't eat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Because the stuff you're eating is completely insubstantial. The only thing substantial is the Soul's influence, which gets more powerful as satiety decreases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 06-17-2015, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:00:31-07:00","id":558899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558882#post558882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not stuck on the ides that it involves actual food. I have previously stated that it does not involve actual food. That has <i>nothing</i> to do with the concept of getting heavier as you eat. You Soul is the thing getting fat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mass has nothing to do with the concept of getting heavier as you eat? Mass is the reason you believe that eating = heavier in the first place.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558882#post558882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You loose all the extra mass at Satiety 10...so? You loose all your Beast powers at Satiety 10, including the other ones that get more powerful as you fill up. There is no thematic issue with this, because it has nothing to do with the themes of a specific power, it affects <i>all</i> powers the same. That would only be relevant if that only happened with this one specific power. It doesn't though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Each one of those facets has a thematic reason for why they stop functioning at Satiety 10, both Atavisms and Nightmares. It is considerably more thematically appropriate that you increase your bestial mass at the same time that you increase your other physical bestial features, instead of getting physically heavier when you treat someone badly or collect a rare book. It is definitely not thematically appropriate to gain a bunch of mass and then suddenly lose it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558882#post558882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are stuck on the idea that it a &quot;should&quot; function s an Atavism. It does not and it should not. The idea of getting heavier when starving is ridiculous and completely counter to the point <i>and</i> theme of the Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>You get <b>more beautiful</b> when you are starving, you get <b>physically stronger</b> when you are starving, you gain <b>more stamina</b> when you are starving, and your <b>skin toughens</b> when you are starving. You know what? You're absolutely right. Getting heavier when starving is <i>ridiculous and completely counter</i> to those things. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:08:31-07:00","id":558906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558535#post558535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think part of the difference of opinion on this is that I'm interpreting this more as the Juggernaut and you (and obviously a number of others) are interpreting it more along the lines of the Blob. (the mutant, not the jello that eats people)</div> </div> </div> </div>Just seeing if I understand this. Juggernaut represents the camp arguing for higher satiety to equal more difficult to stop whereas Blob is representing the lower satiety camp?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:15:25-07:00","id":558912,"title":"","content":"It's not an Atavism though. It's not a defining power/trait of the Soul seeping into the Beast, it's the weight of how full it is manifesting in her flesh. You get denser because you're more full. That makes sense. Getting denser when your metaphysical belly is empty of sweet delicious terror<i> doesn't</i> make sense.<br /> <br /> It runs parallel to Atavisms, not on the same line, so to speak. So their workings don't conflict. Simple as that.<br /> <br /> That's just my opinion though, so like, feel free to disagree or have it work in another way in your games. Even though it internally makes perfect sense as it is, and externally it doesn't contradict Atavisms thematically or mechanically because it's not one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:24:04-07:00","id":558919,"title":"","content":"On a side thing as it is right now I think it combos rather nicely with atavisms like cyclopean strength, unbreakable, or titanic blow. For example an Anakim at high satiety can basically terminator walk through everything to get across the idea of &quot;I am in no rush to get you. You'll tire, you can throw whatever at me and I probably won't even break stride.&quot; Then at low satiety it turns into a freaking cannonball who punches through everything that stands in its way because it has decided it will have the target for lunch now and everything they can throw in the way may as well be a sheets of rice paper for all it will do to stop the Anakim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:24:47-07:00","id":558920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558906#post558906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just seeing if I understand this. Juggernaut represents the camp arguing for higher satiety to equal more difficult to stop whereas Blob is representing the lower satiety camp?</div> </div> </div> </div>I may be wrong, but I believe he means the other way around.<br /> Juggernaut becomes stronger and more durable in the face of adversity.<br /> Blob becomes stronger and more durable when he actually eats.<br /> <br /> For my two cents, Giant (Advanced) should be changed to Lair and be done with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:26:25-07:00","id":558921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558890#post558890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fear does not have a weight. There's no reason why consuming it should make you heavier, except that the <b>Soul is manifesting itself more strongly</b>. The Soul shouldn't be manifesting itself if you're at high satiety.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only thing is says is that as when a Beast is at Satiety 3 or less Atvisms gain a modified effect. There is no mention, or suggestion, that it is due to the Soul being &quot;manifested more strongly&quot;. What it <i>does</i> do is suggest it is due to the Soul being more active. The two are not the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:29:38-07:00","id":558927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558899#post558899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You get <b>more beautiful</b> when you are starving, you get <b>physically stronger</b> when you are starving, you gain <b>more stamina</b> when you are starving, and your <b>skin toughens</b> when you are starving. You know what? You're absolutely right. Getting heavier when starving is <i>ridiculous and completely counter</i> to those things. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because they started by trying to making a Merit more Beastly rather than this is the effect you want and what is the best way to make it happen, that is exactly the thinking. It isn't the only Merit that was Beastified. It is an odd one, but from the starting point that they began from, their method was the most logical. If they did it the other way then it shouldn't be with the Merits. They should have fleshed it out more into an Atavism if they took your approach, &quot;how do we make this happen.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not sure about the terms. The Merit camp uses Blob and the Atavism camp uses Juggernaut. And I think that actually makes it all more confusing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: Actually an Atavism that covered the bolded attributes would be a decent idea. You would definitely be right they increase as Satiety decreases. Interesting enough if they were made as Merits they would still increase as Satiety decreases, except beauty because I don't know what that has to do with anything. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 06-17-2015, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:35:53-07:00","id":558937,"title":"","content":"Or we have the camp of &quot;Its not a problem, it makes perfect sense as is.&quot; Followed by &quot;If you don't like it, then change it in your game.&quot;<br /> <br /> The only thing I argued was &quot;this particular merit is not wrong or a problem and there's no universal need for it to be fixed.&quot; If some people dislike it, that's fine. I disagree with a number of things the writers do. But I wouldn't say its an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-17-2015, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:38:33-07:00","id":558939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558927#post558927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they started by trying to making a Merit more Beastly rather than this is the effect you want and what is the best way to make it happen, that is exactly the thinking. It isn't the only Merit that was Beastified. It is an odd one, but from the starting point that they began from, their method was the most logical. If they did it the other way then it shouldn't be with the Merits. They should have fleshed it out more into an Atavism if they took your approach, &quot;how do we make this happen.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not sure about the terms. The Merit camp uses Blob and the Atavism camp uses Juggernaut. And I think that actually makes it all more confusing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I definitely see that the merit was not a typo or anything. They seemed to go with the Eating = Heavier idea as well. But I don't think they noticed that it broke from the pattern that they had been developing where Starving = More Physical (including attractive) vs Full = More Magical. It doesn't help that no other Beast merit has a similar mechanic, they are all completely static. So we cannot look to them for further guidance or some kind of exception.<br /> <br /> To make another comic book reference, I see it like The Hulk. The angrier he gets (hungrier in this case) the bigger, stronger, tougher, heavier, and more resistant he becomes. The calmer he becomes the weaker he becomes and the more socially vulnerable he becomes. The Hulk doesn't have Nightmares, so that is about where the similarities end =P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:44:25-07:00","id":558943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558939#post558939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, I definitely see that the merit was not a typo or anything. They seemed to go with the Eating = Heavier idea as well. But I don't think they noticed that it broke from the pattern that they had been developing where Starving = More Physical (including attractive) vs Full = More Magical. It doesn't help that no other Beast merit has a similar mechanic, they are all completely static. So we cannot look to them for further guidance or some kind of exception.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why does it matter if it breaks the pattern? Why should they have to adhere to a pattern? I find that particular line of thinking odd. <br /> <br /> Plus, its not like you don't have any benefit from it during Low Satiety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:55:51-07:00","id":558968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558943#post558943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why does it matter if it breaks the pattern? Why should they have to adhere to a pattern? I find that particular line of thinking odd. <br /> <br /> Plus, its not like you don't have any benefit from it during Low Satiety.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanical consistency is important to avoid confusing players. Thematic consistency is important when establishing how things work so that they fit together as a coherent whole. Not everything has to fit into that whole, but each time you break away you need to ask what you gained from doing so. In this case, the gain is nothing.<br /> <br /> Basically, game design theory and KISS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T19:39:24-07:00","id":558996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558920#post558920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be wrong, but I believe he means the other way around.<br /> Juggernaut becomes stronger and more durable in the face of adversity.<br /> Blob becomes stronger and more durable when he actually eats.<br /> <br /> For my two cents, Giant (Advanced) should be changed to Lair and be done with it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are absolutely correct Iry. FWIW changing it to Lair and calling it a day would work perfectly from my POV too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T11:56:19-07:00","id":560998,"title":"","content":"&quot;For my two cents, Giant (Advanced) should be changed to Lair and be done with it.&quot;<br /> <br /> 1.) I think this is the best solution overall.<br /> <br /> 2.) Aside from Nalak42's post &quot;On a side thing as it is right now I think it combos rather nicely with atavisms like cyclopean strength, unbreakable, or titanic blow. For example an Anakim at high satiety can basically terminator walk through everything to get across the idea of &quot;I am in no rush to get you. You'll tire, you can throw whatever at me and I probably won't even break stride.&quot; Then at low satiety it turns into a freaking cannonball who punches through everything that stands in its way because it has decided it will have the target for lunch now and everything they can throw in the way may as well be a sheets of rice paper for all it will do to stop the Anakim.&quot; Which i think is the only decent explanation for why this merit should would work the way it does, i am of the opinion that it should be altered.<br /> <br /> Gallus makes a very good point in that its NOT an atavism and that as such it doesnt have to behave like one, however i still think that overall it feels odd with how it works compared to everything else in the beast book. As an ability that is directly tied to how much physical influence your soul is currently having on your beast, i feel that it should at least behave a little bit in line with how other abilities that are directly tied to how much physical influence your soul has behave. Or at the very least not act in a manner in direct opposition with how they behave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2741-hemophage","name":"Hemophage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T01:22:06-07:00","id":562737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558257-possible-problem-with-the-upgraded-giant-merit-in-beast?p=558920#post558920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For my two cents, Giant (Advanced) should be changed to Lair and be done with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I came on this thread to say pretty much exactly this.<br /> <br /> The only thing I'll note is the scaling may need to be tweaked slightly for that to work, but it's still the best solution I think.","signature":"